<section class="card" aria-labelledby="mission-title">
    <h2 id="mission-title">Mission</h2>
    <p>Students and career-center staff face recruiter emails and offer letters that look legitimate but ask for money, equipment purchases, or personal data. Impersonation of real employers is common, and staff need a shared place to record what they have seen.</p>
    <p>JobLens is a data-grounded assistant for that workflow: check a recruiter, analyze an offer, browse community scam reports, and ask JobLens questions that must be answered from MCP tools over SQLite—not from free-form invention.</p>
    <p>The product is built for a university analytics course (ISM 6225). All report data is sample training data. It is not legal advice and does not accuse real companies of fraud; reports describe impersonation patterns that use company names as cover.</p>
</section>

