<section class="card tech-box" aria-labelledby="tech-title">
    <h2 id="tech-title">Technical details</h2>
    <p class="form-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary"
           href="https://github.com/SathvikReddySirigiri/joblens-chat#readme"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noopener">Read the GitHub README</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary"
           href="https://github.com/SathvikReddySirigiri/joblens-chat/blob/main/docs/DOCUMENTATION.md"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noopener">Full documentation</a>
    </p>

    <h3>External APIs used</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>RDAP</strong> domain registry lookups via hosts such as <code>rdap.org</code> and registry-specific RDAP endpoints (no API key).</li>
        <li><strong>SEC EDGAR</strong> company ticker list from <code>www.sec.gov</code> (public company_tickers.json; User-Agent required).</li>
        <li><strong>Azure OpenAI</strong> chat completions when configured (endpoint host from <code>Ai:Endpoint</code>; key only in user-secrets / App Service settings).</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>CRUD overview</h3>
    <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Entity</th>
                    <th scope="col">Create</th>
                    <th scope="col">Read</th>
                    <th scope="col">Update / Delete</th>
                    <th scope="col">Who</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Scam reports</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                    <td>Yes (visibility by role)</td>
                    <td>Own pending (student); any (moderator)</td>
                    <td>Signed-in students create; moderators approve/reject</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Interview experiences</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                    <td>Own (student); any (moderator)</td>
                    <td>Signed-in users</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Companies</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                    <td>Moderators only</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Recruiters</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                    <td>Moderators only</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Job postings (Jobs → JobLens tab)</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                    <td>Moderators only</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Live openings (Jobs → Live tab)</td>
                    <td>No (fetched on demand)</td>
                    <td>Yes (USAJOBS + trust notes)</td>
                    <td>No</td>
                    <td>Public; not stored in SQLite</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Check logs</td>
                    <td>System</td>
                    <td>Via counts / tools</td>
                    <td>No UI delete</td>
                    <td>Written when checks run</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Users</td>
                    <td>Register (Student)</td>
                    <td>Self via cookie</td>
                    <td>Seed / staff</td>
                    <td>Public register; moderators seeded</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <h3>Data management</h3>
    <p>SQLite file lives under <code>App_Data/joblens.db</code> locally (never under wwwroot) and under a persistent path on Azure. Live row counts:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Companies: @Model.Companies</li>
        <li>ScamReports: @Model.ScamReports (@Model.Approved approved, @Model.Pending pending, @Model.Rejected rejected)</li>
        <li>JobPostings: @Model.JobPostings</li>
        <li>InterviewReviews: @Model.InterviewReviews</li>
        <li>Recruiters: @Model.Recruiters</li>
        <li>CheckLogs: @Model.CheckLogs</li>
        <li>Users: @Model.Users</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Challenges &amp; solutions</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>GitHub Models retired</strong> → switchable AI provider (<code>Demo</code>, Azure OpenAI, OpenAI-compatible).</li>
        <li><strong>Azure quota limits</strong> → choose a deployment/SKU the subscription can host; Demo mode always works without a key.</li>
        <li><strong>RDAP timeouts</strong> → registry-first async client with bounded timeouts and graceful empty panels.</li>
        <li><strong>AI overclaiming “legitimate”</strong> → system prompt requires tool evidence and forbids inventing facts.</li>
        <li><strong>Growing MVC project</strong> → Clean Architecture layers (Domain / Application / Infrastructure / Web) with thin controllers.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="erd-title">
    <h2 id="erd-title">Entity relationship diagram</h2>
    <div class="card mermaid-panel">
        <pre class="mermaid" role="img" aria-label="Entity relationship diagram of JobLens tables">
erDiagram
    COMPANIES ||--o{ SCAMREPORTS : has
    COMPANIES ||--o{ JOBPOSTINGS : has
    COMPANIES ||--o{ INTERVIEWREVIEWS : has
    COMPANIES |o--o{ RECRUITERS : optional
    USERS |o--o{ SCAMREPORTS : CreatedBy
    USERS |o--o{ INTERVIEWREVIEWS : CreatedBy
    COMPANIES {
        int CompanyId PK
        string Name
        string OfficialDomain
        string Industry
        string HqState
    }
    SCAMREPORTS {
        int ReportId PK
        int CompanyId FK
        int CreatedByUserId FK
        string RecruiterEmail
        string Domain
        string Status
    }
    JOBPOSTINGS {
        int PostingId PK
        int CompanyId FK
        string Title
        string PostedDate
    }
    INTERVIEWREVIEWS {
        int ReviewId PK
        int CompanyId FK
        int CreatedByUserId FK
        int Rating
    }
    RECRUITERS {
        int RecruiterId PK
        int CompanyId FK
        string Email
        string Domain
    }
    USERS {
        int UserId PK
        string Email
        string Role
    }
    CHECKLOGS {
        int CheckId PK
        string CheckType
        int RiskScore
        string Verdict
    }
        </pre>
    </div>
    <div class="table-wrap" aria-label="Text alternative for the ERD">
        <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Table</th>
                    <th scope="col">Key columns</th>
                    <th scope="col">Relationships</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Companies</td>
                    <td>CompanyId (PK), Name, OfficialDomain, Industry, HqState</td>
                    <td>Parent of reports, postings, reviews; optional parent of recruiters</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>ScamReports</td>
                    <td>ReportId (PK), CompanyId (FK), CreatedByUserId (FK), Status, Domain</td>
                    <td>Belongs to Companies; optional creator Users</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>JobPostings</td>
                    <td>PostingId (PK), CompanyId (FK), Title, PostedDate</td>
                    <td>Belongs to Companies</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>InterviewReviews</td>
                    <td>ReviewId (PK), CompanyId (FK), CreatedByUserId (FK), Rating</td>
                    <td>Belongs to Companies; optional creator Users</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Recruiters</td>
                    <td>RecruiterId (PK), Email, Domain, CompanyId (FK, nullable)</td>
                    <td>Optional link to Companies</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Users</td>
                    <td>UserId (PK), Email, Role, PasswordHash</td>
                    <td>Owns CreatedBy on reports and reviews</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>CheckLogs</td>
                    <td>CheckId (PK), CheckType, RiskScore, Verdict, CreatedAt</td>
                    <td>Standalone audit of checks</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

